# Independent native Android license scope

This additional MIT grant covers the independently implemented native Android
application in android-native/app/src/main/kotlin, app/src/withCast/kotlin,
app/src/noCast/kotlin and core/src/main/kotlin, the independently maintained
strings and draft translations, independent leaf artwork, and fork-created
Android build configuration and scripts.

Imported upstream translations and launcher artwork are no longer compiled or
bundled. The Material headphones notification vector (ic_small.xml) remains
subject to Google's Apache-2.0 license. Dependencies, Google SDKs, Gradle wrapper
distributions, their notices, legacy exporter/models and migration fixtures are
excluded from this grant and keep their own licenses. Google Cast and Play
Services binaries are proprietary; this grant does not relicense them.

The repository-root GPLv3 license, inherited source and prior release licenses
remain unchanged. Audiobook Loft began as an independent Audiobookshelf fork;
this grant covers owner-controlled replacement code, not upstream rights.

